/-!
# Y12 property-test corpus — Ledger/fold (`applyBlockExec`, the ConnectBlock UTXO fold)

Review-4 support suite contributor Y12, 2026-10-16. NEW file, owned by Y12.

Module under test: `Bitcoin.Ledger` (Interface.lean) — the sequential
block fold `applyBlockExec`/`applyBlockL` with `applyTxStepL`'s check
order (BIP30 duplicate -> HaveInputs -> coinbase maturity -> UpdateCoins),
`updateCoinsL` keying, `addedCoins` (OP_RETURN skip), `maturityOk`,
`bip30Enforced`/`bip30Collision`.

Ground truth: Bitcoin Core @ `cce32b168` (v32.99 pin) — NOT the Lean code:
  * validation.cpp:1998-2011 `UpdateCoins` (spend-all-then-add; coinbase
    exempt from the spend loop), :2401/:2455-2466 BIP30 enforcement
    (`IsBIP30Repeat` :6207 = heights 91842/91880; the BIP34-window hash
    pin is abstracted per the module header; limit 1983702 :2429);
  * coins.cpp:82 `AddCoin` OP_RETURN early return, :133-142 `AddCoins`,
    :322-331 `HaveInputs`;
  * tx_verify.cpp:174 + :185-188 `CheckTxInputs` (missing inputs /
    coinbase maturity), consensus.h:19 `COINBASE_MATURITY = 100`.
The corpus was generated by the plain-python reference
`scratch/Y12/y12ref.py` + `gen.py` (seed 20261016, REPRODUCIBLE; full case
table in `scratch/Y12/cases.json`) and is independent of the Lean
implementation. Every case was ALSO instantiated and re-run with Core's
real sha256d txid keying: all verdicts are key-independent (the keying
seam is only ever compared for equality — see findings-w4/Y12.md).

Sections (all kernel `decide`-checkable concrete vectors):
  S  serTx (txid-preimage) serialization pins vs Core TX_NO_WITNESS
  A  genesis / empty block / empty-tx edges
  B  coinbase maturity edges (depth 99/100/101, same-block, mixed inputs)
  C  double-spend in one block (sequential fold), duplicate tx, dup inputs
  D  OP_RETURN / `IsUnspendable` edges (+ BIP30 collision interaction)
  E  BIP30 height matrix (91842/91880 exempt; BIP34 window; 1983702 limit)
  F  same-block spend ordering (B3): chained spends, wrong order
  G  multi-input / multi-tx assoc-list order pins
  H  pseudo-random tx sequences (fixed seed 20261016)

Result: the Lean fold matches the python reference on every case (green
build); any mismatch would be a findings-w4/Y12.md entry.
-/


